engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:2:## P4. The world's own physics space, and the visitor's body in it.
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:3:##
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:4:## A pack is simulated in a space of its own and must stay untouched. The visitor is not part of any game: he walks the
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:5:## land between them, so the WORLD owns a space (`PhysicsServer3D`, no nodes, no scene tree) that holds only static
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:6:## things, all of them built once:
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:7:##   * the terrain's triangles (a triangle is left out where a plot's own ground carries him instead),
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:8:##   * a wall round every plot's fence, trunks of trees, boulders, the lots' machinery, the bridge,
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:9:##   * for every plot: a COPY of the pack's static colliders (add_pack): the shapes are shared (a shape belongs to no
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:10:##     space), the bodies are new bodies in this space, clipped to the plot's circle and moved to the plot's place with
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:11:##     the same bent rim the draw layer gives the pack's ground. The pack's own bodies are never touched.
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:12:## His own body is a kinematic capsule in that space; `walk()` moves it with the engine's test_motion (slide along what
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:13:## he meets, step up small steps, follow slopes down, refuse slopes steeper than `max_slope_deg`).
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:14:##
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:15:## Nothing here is read by a pack, a scheduler or a state hash: the scripted tour still gives the scheduler the
engine/kernel/world/terrain/world_space.gd:16:## scripted position; the body only decides where the visitor is DRAWN (and, when a person walks, where he is).
