engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:1:extends RefCounted
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:2:## P14. The viewer's (view.gd) work at the seam between a world that builds packs while it is drawn and the visitor:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:3:## the rim cache read before the first frame, and the copy of an arrived pack's colliders into the visitor's space in
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:4:## slices. Static functions on the viewer's own fields (the size rule of `tl arch` keeps view.gd under 600 lines).
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:5:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:6:const DrawScript: GDScript = preload("res://kernel/world/draw/draw.gd")
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:7:const PlotFile: GDScript = preload("res://kernel/world/plotfile.gd")
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:8:const COPY_US: int = 2000               # what the copy may take of a frame
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:9:const COPY_NEAR_M: float = 10.0         # a plot whose edge is nearer than this to the visitor is copied whole at once
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:10:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:11:static var _hashes: Dictionary = {}     # pack directory -> content hash, once per process (PATCHES-P13 entry 4)
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:12:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:13:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:14:## P5. The rim of plot `i` (draw.gd `edge_height`). A plot whose pack is not built yet takes it from the rim cache, a
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:15:## file in the user directory keyed by the pack directory's content, the radius and the scenery; when it is not there
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:16:## the pack is built now, before the first frame, and the cache learns it (the first visit of a world on a machine).
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:17:## P14: a directory's content is hashed once per process, not once per plot (thirty plots of walk30 share nine).
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:18:static func rim_of(v: Node, i: int, r: float) -> float:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:19:	var world: Node = v.get("world")
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:20:	var h: Node = (world.get("packs") as Array)[i]
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:21:	if bool(h.get("loaded")) or world.get("jobs") == null or (h.get("manifest") as Dictionary).is_empty():
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:22:		return float(DrawScript.call("edge_height", h, r))
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:23:	var rims: Dictionary = v.get("_rims")
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:24:	if rims.is_empty() and FileAccess.file_exists(rims_path()):
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:25:		var j: Variant = JSON.parse_string(FileAccess.get_file_as_string(rims_path()))
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:26:		if typeof(j) == TYPE_DICTIONARY:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:27:			rims.merge(j)
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:28:	var dir: String = str(h.get("pack_dir"))
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:29:	if not _hashes.has(dir):
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:30:		_hashes[dir] = str(PlotFile.call("dir_hash", dir))
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:31:	var opts: Dictionary = v.get("opts")
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:32:	var key: String = ("%s|%s|%s" if OS.get_environment("TL_GROUND_COVER") == "off" else "%s|%s|%s|cover") % [str(_hashes[dir]), str(r), str(opts.get("scenery", (world.get("walk") as Dictionary).get("scenery", "plot")))]
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:33:	if not rims.has(key) or OS.get_environment("TL_RIM_CACHE") == "off":
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:34:		(world.get("jobs") as RefCounted).call("now", i)
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:35:		var e: float = float(DrawScript.call("edge_height", (world.get("packs") as Array)[i], r))
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:36:		rims[key] = "none" if is_nan(e) else e
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:37:		v.set("_rims_new", int(v.get("_rims_new")) + 1)
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:38:	return NAN if typeof(rims[key]) == TYPE_STRING else float(rims[key])
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:39:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:40:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:41:static func rims_path() -> String:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:42:	return str(PlotFile.call("cache_dir")) + "/rims.json"          # P14: TL_CACHE_DIR or the user directory
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:43:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:44:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:45:static func save_rims(v: Node) -> void:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:46:	if int(v.get("_rims_new")) == 0:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:47:		return
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:48:	DirAccess.make_dir_recursive_absolute(rims_path().get_base_dir())
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:49:	var f: FileAccess = FileAccess.open(rims_path(), FileAccess.WRITE)
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:50:	if f != null:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:51:		f.store_string(JSON.stringify(v.get("_rims"), "", true))
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:52:		f.close()
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:53:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:54:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:55:## The rule: before the visitor takes a step, every plot whose edge is within COPY_NEAR_M of him has all its
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:56:## colliders (copied whole now if it must); of the rest the nearest is copied for COPY_US a frame. Running (9 m/s) he
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:57:## covers 10 m in 66 ticks; a seed's copy (5 ms whole) takes three slices. Returns the microseconds it took.
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:58:static func copy_colliders(copies: Array, ws: Object, plots: Array, radii: Array, at: Vector3) -> int:
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:59:	var tc: int = Time.get_ticks_usec()
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:60:	var best: int = -1
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:61:	var best_d: float = INF
engine/kernel/world/draw/view_seam.gd:62:	for k: int in range(copies.size() - 1, -1, -1):
