   1 extends RefCounted
   2 ## P5. The build queue of a scheduled world (kernel/world/world.gd owns one; TIERS.md "Loading" has the model and
   3 ## the measured numbers). Loading is not simulation: a pack that is still being built is `unbuilt` for the scheduler,
   4 ## and the tick boundary it arrives on is an event (`built`) in the world log, so a replay does the same.
   5 ##
   6 ## A pack is built in two parts:
   7 ##   PREPARE  on this queue's worker thread: every script of the pack is loaded (parsed and compiled) and every
   8 ##            `tl.layout/1` file under its data/ is built ahead by the kit (TLKit.build_layout_ahead: the venue's
   9 ##            meshes, bodies and rigs, off the scene tree). This is 95 to 99 % of a seed's loading time.
  10 ##   ATTACH   on the main thread, at a tick boundary: the holder is made, `_pack_setup` runs (its `build_layout`
  11 ##            calls find the layouts built ahead and only attach them), the laws are applied. The pack's first tick
  12 ##            is the next one (the one-tick rest of N7).
  13 ## Order: the tier first (stage, sideline, backdrop), then the distance to the player. A plot in `ledger` is not built.
  14 ##
  15 ## Modes (tiers.json `load.mode`; the walk or `--load=` may override):
  16 ##   queue  attach what is ready, at least one pack per tick, more while this tick's attaches used less than
  17 ##          `load.budget_ms`. The arrival tick depends on the machine: for a world somebody looks at.
  18 ##   step   one pack per world tick in queue order, built whole on the main thread (the worker is not used: it would
  19 ##          only be waited for): the arrival tick is a pure function of the walk (time is physics frames). For
  20 ##          scripted runs without a window.
  21 ##   wait   as step, but prepared on the worker and waited for: the worker's path with arrival ticks that do not
  22 ##          depend on the machine (the selftest case world.queue; a window-less run is over before a worker is done).
  23 ##   auto   `queue` in a window, `step` without one. `block` (no queue at all: every pack before the first tick,
  24 ##          as before P5) is handled by world.gd: it makes no queue.
  25 ## No global class name is used here.
  26 
  27 const PackScript: GDScript = preload("res://kernel/world/pack.gd")
  28 const PlotFile: GDScript = preload("res://kernel/world/plotfile.gd")
