 206 ## Walker-feel T (blink B1): the share of the plot's rim that the pack's own wide meshes really cover. The world's
 207 ## ground is cut open to radius + 2.5 m for a pack with ground of its own; ex_car's ground is two boxes 60 m wide
 208 ## (its plot is 80 m across) and the 400 m ice box stands with its origin 200 m out, so the plot cut drops it whole:
 209 ## the corners of the boxes reached the rim ring and the hole was cut, and most of the plot showed the sky.
 210 ## Points on two circles (radius - 2 and radius + 2, 72 each) count as covered when a wide mesh that the plot cut
 211 ## keeps (its origin inside the radius) spans them in x and z. TL_GROUND_COVER=off: the rule before (the before
 212 ## pictures; the rim cache then uses the key without "|cover").
 213 const COVER_MIN: float = 0.95
 214 
