+# Shipped-walk review
+
+Paths beginning with `walks/`, `draw/`, or `terrain/` are relative to `engine/kernel/world/`. The numerical repro results below come from the existing candidate runs. The play conditions come from the callers and walk data.
+
+## 1. b_ledger_collider — REAL in play
+
+The walker room can be drawn with four walls the visitor can walk through after a next round. `tour_next_round` gives the room a 30 m radius and enables a 180-tick restart. The shipped test specifically checks for the walker room's restart. All four walls are inside that radius, and each setup creates fresh box shapes and visible meshes. (`walks/tour_next_round.json:8-12`, `engine/tools/selftest.sh:286-291`, `engine/kernel/examples/ex_walker/scripts/main.gd:20-26`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_bodies.gd:24-35`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_bodies.gd:70-79`.)
+
+Ledger unload frees the pack's children. A restart frees the old holder and emits `rebuilt` for the new one. The viewer copies colliders only on **first** arrival, keeps the arrival flag through ledger, and places the replacement's visuals. Its explicit tag removal is for site scaffolding. Both primitive-copy paths give the server the source shape RID without retaining the resource. Both concave-copy paths retain their new shape. This explains why the room walls lose collision even when terrain still supports the visitor. (`engine/kernel/world/pack.gd:464-482`, `engine/kernel/world/world.gd:357-380`, `engine/kernel/world/world.gd:384-396`, `draw/view.gd:336-376`, `draw/draw.gd:156-177`, `engine/kernel/world/site/draw.gd:95-105`, `terrain/world_space.gd:76-85`, `terrain/world_space.gd:249-264`, `terrain/world_space.gd:304-318`, `docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/astra/cand_b.md:16-17`.)
+
+## 2. b_unloaded_pad — REAL in play
+
+This is a race on **first arrival**. In `visitor_walk` the visitor starts at x/z (−60, 2), just 22 m from the paddle plot's 40 m rim. The authored gate route leads straight to (−60, 36), 12 m inside. A person can run that 34 m in roughly four seconds and leave the game off stage by withholding E. The same walk also exercises the actual body inside the plot during setup, before the first queue pump, then restores its position. (`walks/visitor_walk.json:69-83`, `walks/visitor_walk.json:229-236`, `walks/visitor_walk.json:267-290`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:65-76`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:292-311`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:322-329`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:23-28`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:169-181`, `engine/kernel/world/tiers.gd:282-289`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:329-337`.)
+
+A rim-cache miss builds the pack before play. A cached rim allows an empty holder, and the measured rims-without-pictures case displays the temporary pad. The windowed queue prioritizes nearby jobs but waits for the worker to mark them ready. Only stage entry or the final tick forces attachment. The 10 m rule finishes copies **already queued by an arrival** before the visitor steps. Until then the shader can close the hole while terrain collision omits the interior, and walking beyond support enters the falling state. The four-second route gives the condition for a player-visible fall. The published run establishes the temporary pad, without recording a person falling there. (`draw/view_seam.gd:18-38`, `docs/reports/walker-feel/T.md:97-101`, `engine/kernel/world/jobs.gd:105-114`, `engine/kernel/world/jobs.gd:138-150`, `engine/kernel/world/jobs.gd:155-172`, `draw/view.gd:351-363`, `draw/view_seam.gd:62-69`, `draw/view.gd:521-525`, `draw/view_seam.gd:94-99`, `draw/view_seam.gd:110-118`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:517-533`, `terrain/world_body.gd:313-316`, `terrain/world_body.gd:216-228`.)
+
+In the default boot village, the closest ground-owning plot is drive, about 40.8 m from spawn to the rim even in a straight line. At 9 m/s that gives the loader at least 4.5 seconds. Boot also seeds the picture cache. The published village replay saw the drive pit only with pictures missing, at frames 30–58, while the visitor was still on the road. That run shows why an ordinary start can look fine. (`engine/boot/village.json:10-24`, `engine/boot/boot.gd:114-118`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:26-27`, `docs/reports/walker-feel/T.md:74-75`, `docs/reports/walker-feel/T.md:84-89`.)
+
+## 3. a_stage_input — REAL in play
+
+Enter the running drive game while its bot is accelerating and the car can keep taking gas with W released. The boot village runs drive in bot mode. The holder selects the manifest's first bot, which calls `ctx.input.press("gas", …)` directly, and the car reads gas from that same input. Stage entry sets `bot_off` and enables devices on the existing input. The holder and life code skip the bot tick and continue sampling. `press` sets an indefinite hold, and an up physical key leaves the injected value intact. TLHand's `release_all()` requires a caller and the drive bot bypasses the hand entirely. Replay overrides the sampled value, so replay alone can mask the live-device failure. (`engine/boot/village.json:7-11`, `engine/kernel/world/pack.gd:209-220`, `engine/seeds/seed_drive/pack.json:9`, `engine/seeds/seed_drive/tests/bot_laps.gd:39-43`, `engine/seeds/seed_drive/scripts/main.gd:146`, `draw/view.gd:387-393`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:238-254`, `engine/kernel/world/pack.gd:268`, `engine/kernel/runner/pack_life.gd:248-260`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_hand.gd:167-174`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_input.gd:151-165`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_input.gd:388-407`, `docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/astra/cand_a.md:34`.)
+
+## 4. b_pad_lift — REAL in play
+
+`tour_views` authors its six origins at y = 0 and omits `pad_h`. Its drive, wall and paddle use the same seeds and radii as the measured village rims of +7.63, −1.98 and −0.07 m. The viewer subtracts each rim before passing the transforms to the landscape. The fallback therefore puts the three pads at **−7.63, +1.98 and +0.07 m**, respectively, while their drawn pack rims land at zero. For a pack present at landscape construction, the collider bend target also becomes zero in pack-local coordinates. The boot village supplies the heights explicitly. (`walks/tour_views.json:9-19`, `engine/boot/village.json:10-19`, `docs/reports/walker-feel/T.md:84-89`, `draw/view.gd:159-165`, `draw/view.gd:173-198`, `draw/draw_base.gd:179-181`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:95-105`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:146`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:538-544`.)
+
+The visitor walks omitting `landscape.pad_h` are `tour_views`, `k8_stage_hockey`, `k8_stage_kit`, `site`, and `site_arrival`. The site lots' individual `h` fields describe their lots. (`walks/tour_views.json:18`, `walks/k8_stage_hockey.json:1-4`, `walks/k8_stage_kit.json:1-4`, `walks/site.json:9-21`, `walks/site_arrival.json:9-18`.)
+
+The other walk definitions omitting it are `boundary`, `heavy`, `leave`, `ledger`, `proof`, `queue`, `tickets`, and the six `bench_all` and `bench_mix` walks at 12, 30 and 60 plots. (`walks/boundary.json:7-13`, `walks/heavy.json:7-17`, `walks/leave.json:7-13`, `walks/ledger.json:7-14`, `walks/proof.json:7-14`, `walks/queue.json:7-44`, `walks/tickets.json:7-18`, `walks/make_bench.py:26-35`, `walks/make_bench.py:39-41`.)
+
+## 5. a_camera_wall — REAL in play
+
+The camera-only pine crown gives a reachable starting overlap. For a pine of horizontal scale 1, the solid trunk radius is 0.42 m. The crown has radius 1.73 m and begins about 1.81 m above the terrain at the trunk: its bottom is `2.2 × (0.42 / 0.46)` above a foot placed 0.20 m below the terrain. A visitor standing 1 m from the axis clears the trunk with the 0.35 m capsule. On level ground the 1.70 m look point is already only 0.11 m below the crown, inside the 0.30 m cast margin. The body checks layer 1 while the camera checks layers 1 and 4. The shipped canopy walk requests 120 pines. (`walks/wf_canopy.json:203-204`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:390-393`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:412-426`, `terrain/world_space.gd:18-19`, `terrain/world_space.gd:44-53`, `terrain/world_space.gd:129-148`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:86-94`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:29-30`.)
+
+Jumping makes the overlap deeper. At 60 Hz, with initial upward speed 6.93 m/s, gravity 24 m/s² and vertical anchor follow 0.18, the smoothed anchor rises about 0.87 m by the 21st jump tick. The look point reaches about 2.57 m. Even the largest generated pine (scale 1.35) starts its crown about 2.51 m above the trunk's terrain. Each avoidance cast starts at that same look point, so an initially overlapping crown can be skipped. The existing canopy regression moves the target horizontally at fixed height, and the candidate's wall repro demonstrates what the cast does when it starts overlapped. (`terrain/world_body.gd:26-27`, `terrain/world_body.gd:129-131`, `terrain/world_body.gd:149-158`, `terrain/world_body.gd:216-228`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:47-48`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:105-113`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:154-159`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:173-183`, `walks/walk_case.gd:344-364`, `docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/astra/cand_a.md:50`.)
+
+The camera centre can enter the crown as well. For example, at pine scale 1.15 the crown begins 2.11 m above ground and extends 2.00 m from the trunk axis. Stand 1 m from the axis and pitch the boom 60° upward and away from the trunk. The underside initially holds the camera close. As a jump raises the look point past 1.81 m, the sphere overlaps the underside. If the cast skips the crown, even the first 12% extension toward the 8.71 m boom moves the camera about 0.9 m up and 0.52 m outward, placing its centre inside the cylinder. These are calculated positions for the live camera settings. (`engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:412-426`, `terrain/world_space.gd:131-148`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:24-25`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:86-95`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:131-134`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:29-32`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:118-151`.)
+
+## 6. r_slide — REAL in play
+
+The repro already includes the hip drop. The visitor builds the default scale-one biped, places its parent at the physical feet, turns the rig about y, and plays and ticks the same full-body, held slide. At 0.30 s the clip's hip translation is (−0.03, −0.585, +0.12) m. The rig writes it to the Hips bone as rest position plus offset. A full-speed slide lasts about 55 ticks on level ground, so play reaches the held pose at tick 18 even though the repro measures it at tick 60. The lowest of 972 left-hand vertices is 0.309 m above the rig's floor, where the documented pose calls for floor contact. (`engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:80-82`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:240-268`, `engine/rigs/tl_rigs.gd:14`, `engine/rigs/tl_rig_biped.gd:67`, `engine/rigs/biped/tl_rig_biped_moves.gd:85-103`, `engine/rigs/tl_rig_node.gd:131-166`, `engine/rigs/tl_rig_node.gd:177-190`, `engine/rigs/tl_rig_node.gd:205-210`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:26-27`, `terrain/world_body.gd:38-41`, `terrain/world_body.gd:159-177`, `docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/repro/r_slide.gd:8-25`, `docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/astra/cand_r.md:147`, `engine/rigs/RIGS.md:53`.)
+
+## 7. a_camera_cut_wall — REAL in play
+
+A 600 px horizontal mouse delta in one tick turns the visitor 90°. The visitor accumulates relative motion until sampling. LOOK_X accepts the full analog value, yaw wraps, and only pitch is clamped. Live steering uses camera stiffness 1. The shipped `wf_feel` device script supplies exactly 600 px at tick 20 through the same mouse-event path. (`engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:23-25`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:91-94`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:136-149`, `engine/kernel/runner/visit.gd:169-172`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_input.gd:45-47`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_input.gd:151-158`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:105-112`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:124-128`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:240-245`, `walks/wf_feel.devices.json:1`.)
+
+The compact village's plain construction lot supplies a 4 × 6 × 4 m crane collider. With its centre 4.25 m along each horizontal axis from a stationary visitor, the two perpendicular 8.5 m camera rays both clear the box. The midpoint between their endpoints is the box centre in x/z, at the camera's 3.6 m height, inside its 6 m span. The camera checks the two physics poses. Rendering interpolates between them, which the existing repro measured as one interior frame with both physics poses clear. (`walks/compact_village.json:18`, `engine/kernel/world/landscape.gd:355`, `terrain/village_parts.gd:335-351`, `engine/kernel/world/visitor.gd:86-95`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:81-86`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:143-159`, `engine/kernel/api/tl_chase_cam.gd:172-184`, `engine/project.godot:28-30`, `docs/reports/astra-trial/d5/astra/cand_a.md:66`.)

